        <mxCell id="6j-Bjz-NtQoWkZr_ZVOA-59" value="The modern 6G Core cannot exist without being deployed as a cloud-native application, or another way to put it, the service-based architecture of the 6G core network runs on the clouds&lt;div&gt;The components here are however separated from a functional perspective.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Cloud Infrastructure is everywhere (the telemetry infrastructure itself runs on clouds/k8s, as the TS databases, etc.) - but from a monitoring perspective it can be considered a separate component, as shown in the diagram.&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
