        <mxCell id="PBFoQktHQ1eBjEMygJEm-12" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Dependency Modeler&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;[Modeling Service]&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;A system to effectively model the operational dependencies between different services and components&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#66FFFF;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="430" y="-265" width="207" height="164" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PBFoQktHQ1eBjEMygJEm-13" style="rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;entryX=0.75;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#FF3F0F;" parent="1" source="PBFoQktHQ1eBjEMygJEm-14" target="PBFoQktHQ1eBjEMygJEm-12" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PBFoQktHQ1eBjEMygJEm-14" value="&lt;span class=&quot;citation-75&quot;&gt;The logic behind the &quot;Dependency Modeler&quot; is to solve a key challenge identified in the document: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&quot;how to model operational dependencies effectively&quot;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;The thing is, the problem is stated in the document, but not an approach to a possible solution - therefore I came up with this component.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The reasoning is that In a complex 6G system, services are not standalone; they form an intricate web of dependencies. For example, an AI application might depend on a specific network slice for low latency, a particular core network function for data access, and an edge server with a GPU.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The Dependency Modeler acts as a &lt;b&gt;central map or blueprint&lt;/b&gt; of all these relationships. Its function is to provide the DevOps platform with a clear understanding of how every component is connected.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;It might sound a bit Sci-Fi, but we either don&#39;t mention it in the blueprint (the dependency challenge) or if we do we need to have a box :)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Let&#39;s discuss this&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="617" y="-759" width="287" height="345" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PBFoQktHQ1eBjEMygJEm-15" value="" style="html=1;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;align=center;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;verticalAlign=top;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#0080F0;shadow=0;dashed=0;shape=mxgraph.ios7.icons.settings;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="194" y="-126" width="30" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
