        <mxCell id="PBFoQktHQ1eBjEMygJEm-33" value="&lt;div&gt;Page 29 and Page 56 on the blueprint architecture do mention DevSecOps, also as KPI - so this seems to be the most logical place&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;snippet from the blueprint:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;....For the FNS project an important aspect is to provide a Secure DevSecOps platform that facilitates the&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;development of services and core network components. This platform should provide tooling and&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;mechanisms to check for security issues before services are deployed in the core network infrastructure....&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;align=left;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" parent="1" vertex="1">
